Building and installing Bells
=============================

Bells 0.8.7.1 builds two executables:

    bellsd      headless daemon (JSON-RPC server, mining node)
    bells-qt    graphical wallet (Qt 5)

End users on Windows do not need to build anything: unpack the release archive
and run `bells-qt.exe` or `bellsd.exe`. See README.md, section
"Getting started (Windows)".

Building from source
--------------------

Read the platform specific notes before starting:

    doc/build-msw.md    Windows: cross-compile from Linux (verified for 0.8.7.1),
                        native MSYS2 builds are documented as well
    doc/build-unix.md   Linux and other Unix-like systems
    doc/build-osx.md    macOS

Required libraries:

    Boost           1.83 is known to work (newer versions may need patches)
    Berkeley DB     4.8.30.NC, required for wallet compatibility
    OpenSSL         1.0.2u, required by the 0.8.x API
    LevelDB         bundled in src/leveldb, no separate install needed
    Qt              5.15.2, only needed for the graphical wallet
    miniupnpc       optional, UPnP support

The 0.8.x code base predates the OpenSSL 1.1 API and does not build against
OpenSSL 3.x. OpenSSL 1.0.2u has to be built and linked explicitly; the same
applies to Boost, which must be built with a C++11 compiler and linked
statically on Windows.

Daemon build (Unix-like systems):

    cd src
    make -f makefile.unix

Daemon build (cross-compile for Windows):

    cd src
    make -f makefile.linux-mingw

Note: `makefile.linux-mingw` uses the historical library names
(`boost_*-mt-s`). With a Boost installation built using `--layout=system`
adjust `BOOST_LIB_SUFFIX` and `LDFLAGS` accordingly, or follow the step by step
instructions in doc/build-msw.md.

Graphical wallet build:

    qmake bitcoin-qt.pro
    make

Installation
------------

The build does not provide an install target. Deployment consists of copying
the executables together with their runtime dependencies:

    Windows   bellsd.exe, bells-qt.exe, Qt5*.dll, libwinpthread-1.dll,
              libstdc++-6.dll, libgcc_s_*.dll, platforms/qwindows.dll,
              imageformats/, styles/
    Unix      bellsd, bells-qt and the system Qt/Boost/OpenSSL libraries

Prebuilt Windows archives are published on the GitHub releases page:
`bells-0.8.7.1-win64.zip` and `bells-0.8.7.1-win32.zip`.
